    "commit": "7d0ca6c1325043466a4cb95b1db354a8956e6ff5",
    "note": "Merge of the MeloNX lot 9 handoff (work/melonx-fps-stability-20261103 a8198f79), no conflict. Brings: build-utils/melonx/moltenvk/rewindbox-drawable-ownership.patch pinned in moltenvk-rebuild.json (present owns its drawable, KhronosGroup/MoltenVK#2791); MeloNXSkinInteraction and the session change that give skin touches back after the in-game menu, with their simulator tests; the Core 719 candidate (adapt_bgc_fragmentation_guard, contract 38b3a5b7, plan, verifier, gates and receipts); MeloNXPerfJournal mgd= field. Independent read-only review: no proven defect; one consequence of the guard relayed to its owner (keep-alive silent after a long fragmented skip)."
   },
   {
    "commit": "80aa7ac75e3fe1559270d34b4701efd00c4fa12b",
    "note": "Merge of PR 166 (work/skins-screen-framing-20261110 32fd5309): screens[0].screenCutout and outputFrame measured on each Pocket body by tools/skins/screen_opening.py, six archives and the catalog rebuilt, the body masked by the cutout in the Dolphin, ARMSX2 and MeloNX skin overlays, Dolphin lockRenderSurface sized for the settled bounds. One conflict resolved by keeping both imports of MeloNXSkinOverlayTests.mm. Independent read-only review of the native code: nothing to correct."
   },
   {
    "commit": "b6a9deee9f307f2d3656e7e91d9c96fa74730be9",
    "note": "Merge of PR 167 (work/skins-realistic-press-20261110 66c129b9, stacked on 166), no conflict: only the pressed sprites of the three Originals and of Switch Pocket change, with their four archives and catalog identities."
   },
   {
    "commit": "b179a080a42ec51ecf1ea62842023686e8696f7f",
    "note": "MoltenVK rebuild pin moved to run 42760131591 (binary 6d3a8d03, patch 9a6867b7) after the artifact was verified offline; package_standalone_moltenvk.py accepts a pinned patch only when pin, source and artifact agree and writes the modification notice with a copy of the patch; parity test 64 checks."
   },
   {
    "commit": "c6cb583707088f6b167b3a5d84ca2a61627657f6",
    "note": "Pocket skin revision review for the six packs rebuilt by PR 166 and PR 167 (docs/evidence/pocket-skins-framing-press-declarations-2026-11-10.json, chained to the Switch Pocket review) and its rule in collect_build_source_evidence.py: an earlier review accepts a rebuilt pack only at the identity the revision gives it, when the revision names the identity that review recorded. Contract test with six negative controls."
   }
